PUBLIC SCHOOL FOUNDATION PROGRAM ACCOUNT $5,805,000
Description of appropriation:
This bill creates a mental health program for K-12 public education, appropriating
$5,580,000 for grants to Wyoming public school districts and $225,000 for the
Department of Education to hire two new full-time positions.
The bill directs each participating school district to create community project
manager and community support coordinator positions. A district's community project
manager position's salary and fringe benefits shall not exceed $100,000 per year
for districts with 500 or more students and shall not exceed $25,000 per year for
districts with less than 500 students. A district's community support coordinator
position's salary and fringe benefits shall not exceed $35,000 per year.
FY 2026 FY 2027 FY 2028
